<%= render "style" %><main class="lm"><h1>Application sending key</h1><p>This key can send from <strong><%= @account.address %></strong>. Copy it now; it will not be shown again. Keep it in the client’s Vault, never in browser code.</p><pre><%= @token %></pre><h2>HTTPS submission</h2><p>Use POST <code>https://lightekmcg.com/api/lightek-mail/messages</code> with these headers:</p><pre>Authorization: Bearer YOUR_MAILBOX_KEY
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: UNIQUE_REQUEST_ID</pre><pre>{"to":"recipient@example.com","subject":"Hello","text":"A message from Lightek."}</pre><p>A 202 response means queued. Poll the returned status URL with the same authorization header. Retry a timed-out HTTP request with the same idempotency key. “Sent” means SMTP acceptance, not verified delivery to the recipient.</p><%= link_to "Back to mailbox", dashboard_mail_path(account_id: @account.id) %></main>
